edian (9%), a real cost or pricing edge over peers.","Its share of sector profits slightly exceeds its share of revenue (1.44x).","It accounts for 1.9% of sector revenue and 2.7% of sector operating profit.","Over five years it has been gaining share of the sector profit pool (+7.4% a year).","The sector is fragmented and competitive (HHI 0.06 across 169 companies in the universe; the top four hold 36% of revenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares are in a steep downtrend, down 37% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits near the bottom of its 52-week range, 46% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 36% and a beta of 1.26, it amplifies market moves, though its beta has shifted (1y 0.47 vs 5y 1.40), so read it loosely.","Liquidity is deep, with about $2.4B traded a day.","In past sell-offs it fell 23% in the 2020 crash, 72% in the 2022 bear market and 56% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $42.68 (margin of safety -49%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models corroborate one another (dispersion 2%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $31.00 to $59.53 (P10-P90).","On multiples it looks expensive against Communication Services peers: EV/EBITDA 17.5 vs 9.4 and P/FCF 27.5 vs 11.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is cheap: the EBIT multiple sits 54% below its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.6% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 4.8% (vs the 8% bar).","The 43 covering analysts target $84.76 on average, 34% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 24% clears the cost of capital of 10.7% by 14pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.83).","It runs a 36% gross margin and converts 21% of revenue into free cash flow.","ROE of 41% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.1x equity multiplier).","Operating margin is running 13pp above its own historical average, a peak-margin risk if conditions normalise.","It spends 7.5% of revenue on R&D and 0.8% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.4x net debt to EBITDA ($9.1B of cash against $14.5B of debt), with interest covered 17.2x."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 12.6% over 3 years, 12.6% over 5 years and 20.9% over 10 years.","Net reinvestment is nil (capex and working capital no more than cover depreciation), so fundamental growth is near zero.","Free cash flow has compounded 37.4% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.1% trend).","Forward indicators: deferred revenue up 17%.","Capex runs 2.1x depreciation (1.5% of sales), so it is building capacity for future growth."],"own":["Insiders hold little stock (0.6%), and institutions hold 85%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (9 sales, net $4.1M sold).","It returns 3.5% a year to shareholders (3.5% in buybacks).","The share count has shrunk 1.5% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 16,000 employees, each generates about $2.8M of revenue, 4.6x the Communication Services median, and productivity has risen 22.9% a year.","That works out to $591K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $12.5M (4x revenue per employee).","Stock compensation averages $23K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":71,"head":"Avoid: priced 49% above its fair value of $42.68.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 56, gates 16/25)","ROIC 24.5% vs WACC 10.7%","FCF margin 20.9%","Revenue grew 12.6%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.4x"],"cons":["Trades 49% above fair value of $42.68","EV/EBITDA 17.5x vs sector 9.4x","P/FCF 27.5x vs sector 11.3x","12-1 month momentum -37%"],"flags":["Priced 49% above its fair value of $42.68"],"need":[],"buy_below":36.28,"vc":{"base":42.68,"base_src":"dcf","bear":31.0,"bull":59.53,"alt_median":27.3,"n_alt":2,"gap":0.5635,"dispersion":0.0221,"level":"LOW","why":["DCF is 56% abo